EvdevTouchParser.java and PressTriggerDetector.java are transplanted from references/MMGG, package com.leaf.hyperdragshare.codex, with package changes and attribution headers. The former MMGG node classifier and candidate selector have been replaced by EVO's shared screen-content recognition. EvdevTouchParser additionally retains a pending tracking start until split-frame X/Y coordinates arrive and uses final-frame coordinates on release (covered by EVO regression tests). Reference regression tests are transplanted with package/runtime changes; additional tests are EVO additions.

RootTouchSource, PressCaptureSource, RootNodeCaptureMain, BackgroundTouchBlocker, AccessibilityBlacklist, OverlayTouchRegions, GestureMath and DragShareController inform the adapted EVO implementation. The input transport uses a Shizuku shell getevent PFD stream; node lookup uses EVO's shared accessibility recognition, with screenshots only for recognized image regions and no OCR fallback. Text and visible image regions both enter EVO's existing drop panel, intentionally replacing MMGG's default text segmentation. Background touch cancellation uses a guarded Shizuku DOWN/CANCEL injection sequence; no LSPosed host, Root node capture, MMGG OCR fallback or click replay is included.
